<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince Henry the Navigator</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1394">1394</a>–<a href="/years/1460">1460</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Prince Henry, Henry's</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Henry the Navigator was a fifteenth-century Portuguese prince, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-of-portugal">King João I</a>, who took part in the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a> in 1415. He sponsored a series of expeditions down the West African coast and promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> cultivation on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madeira">Madeira</a>. His patronage turned exploration into a systematic enterprise and laid the foundations of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator.jpg" alt="Prince Henry the Navigator" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nuno Gonçalves · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henry_the_Navigator1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
